---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../components/SectionHeading.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { withBase } from '../utils/paths';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About an aerospace and mechanical engineer focused on traceable analysis, hardware, verification, and communication."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="shell page-hero-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="page-hero-index">01 / PROFILE</span>
        <h1>Engineering at the boundary of analysis and hardware.</h1>
      </div>
      <div class="page-hero-note">
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-pad">
    <div class="shell about-intro-grid">
      <aside class="about-aside">
        <dl>
          <div>
            <dt>Education</dt>
            <dd>Aerospace Engineering <br />
                Mechanical Engineering <br />
                Applied Physics
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Location</dt>
            <dd>{site.location}</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Working style</dt>
            <dd>Analytical <br />
                Collaborative <br />
                Hardware Focus
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Portfolio scope</dt>
            <dd>Sanitized public examples</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </aside>

      <div class="prose-large">
        <p class="eyebrow">Profile</p>
        <h2>I thrive making complicated systems legible.</h2>
        <p>
          My experience and education have provided me the opportunity to hone my passion of solving
          complex problems with clear and concise documentation. When a problem arises I derive explicit requirements,
          bound assumptions, observable evidence, and a mathematical model to represent each case. With all this clearly
          displayed, my engineering team can make reasonable and informed decisions. 
        </p>
        <p>
          There is always room to grow, and I continue to learn new methods, better understand the consequences of technical 
          decisions, and develop broader engineering perspectives every day. However, I feel I am approaching a plateau 
          in my growth within mechanical hardware development. I want to continue this trajectory of technical growth by 
          transitioning into the fusion-energy sector. I am seeking a highly technical role involving complex analytical, 
          mechanical, and multiphysics challenges. The opportunity to apply my experience toward reliable, low-carbon 
          electricity generation strongly aligns with my professional motivations.
        </p>
        <p>
          This portfolio provides evidence of the capabilities I would bring to that transition. In addition to my education 
          and professional experience, it includes representative projects, engineering tools, and technical writing. 
          To respect confidentiality, program names, organizations, numerical results, and proprietary details are omitted 
          unless they appear in approved public sources. Relevant public material associated with my work is presented on the 
          News page.
        </p>
        <p>
          Outside engineering, I enjoy nature photography and exploring through hiking. Natural environments provide 
          endless opportunities to observe complex systems and test assumptions—from cloud dynamics and geological 
          formations to desert ecology. These systems are governed by the same fundamental physical principles applied in 
          space hardware and fusion engineering, expressed at different scales and through different mechanisms.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

   </BaseLayout>
